jecture on the regularity of binomial edge ideals in full generality.\\n\\n## Keywords\\n\\nBinomial edge ideals\\n\\nCastelnuovo-Mumford regularity\\n\\nCompatible maps\\n\\nClique disjoint edge sets\\n\\n© 2021 Elsevier Inc.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nA proof for a conjecture on the regularity of binomial edge ideals (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0097316521000315)\\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # A proof for a conjecture on the regularity of binomial edge ideals ... Now, we are ready to state our first main theorem that establishes a general upper bound for the regularity of binomial edge ideals. ... arXiv:1906.05510 (2019) ... On the binomial edge ideal of a pair of graphs\\n\\n# A proof for a conjecture on the regularity of binomial edge ideals\\n\\nAuthor links open overlay panel Mohammad Rouzbahani Malayeri ^{a}, Sara Saeedi Madani ^{a} ^{b}, Dariush Kiani ^{a} ^{b}\\n\\nShow more\\n\\nView PDFDownload full issue\\n\\nCite\\n\\nAdd to Mendeley\\n\\nShare\\n\\n10.1016/j.jcta.2021.105432\\n\\nMore actions\\n\\n  * Article\\n  * Recommended articles\\n  * Cited by (15)\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nIn this paper we introduce the concept of clique disjoint edge sets in graphs. Then, for a graph G, we define the invariant as the maximum size of a clique disjoint edge set in G. We show that the regularity of the binomial edge ideal of G is bounded above by . This, in particular, settles a conjecture on the regularity of binomial edge ideals in full generality.\\n\\n## Keywords\\n\\nBinomial edge ideals\\n\\n;\\n\\nCastelnuovo-Mumford regularity\\n\\n;\\n\\nCompatible maps\\n\\n;\\n\\nClique disjoint edge sets\\n\\n\\n## 1. Introduction\\n\\nThroughout the paper, all graphs are assumed to be simple (i.e. with no direction, loops and multiple edges).\\n\\nLet G be a graph on the vertex set and the edge set . Let also be the polynomial ring over a field \\\\mathbb{K}. Then, the binomial edge ideal associated to G, denoted by {J}_{G}, is the ideal in S generated by all the quadratic binomials of the form , where and . This class of ideals was introduced in [7] and [16], as a natural generalization of determinantal ideals, as well as the ideals generated by the adjacent 2-minors of a -matrix of indeterminates.\\n\\nIn the meantime, many researchers have studied the algebraic properties and homological invariants of binomial edge ideals. A main goal is to understand how the invariants and properties of the ideal and the underlying graph are related, see e.g. [1], [2], [3], [4], [5], [6], [11], [14], [15], [19], [20], [21], [22] for some efforts in this direction.\\n\\nOne of the most interesting homological invariants associated to binomial edge ideals that has attracted much attention is the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity, (or regularity for simplicity), namely,\\n\\nIn [20], the second and third authors of the present paper, characterized the graphs G for which . They also gave a characterization of the graphs G with , in [22]. Another important result about the regularity of this class of binomial ideals appeared in [15], where the authors showed that where denotes the sum of the lengths of longest induced paths of connected components of G. Recently, the upper bound has been slightly improved in [5]. In [15] the authors additionally conjectured that , if G is not {P}_{n}, the path on n vertices. Later, in [11], this conjecture was proved by the second and the third authors of this paper. On the other hand, in [20] it was shown that , for the so-called closed graphs (also known as proper interval graphs), where denotes the number of maximal cliques of G. Afterwards, in 2013, the following conjecture regarding the regularity of binomial edge ideals was posed by the second and third authors of this paper, (see [21, page 12] and [11, Conjecture A]).\\n## 2. Upper bounds for the regularity of binomial edge ideals\\n\\nIn this section